  "source_id": "county-059",
  "text": "McDowell County Board of Elections \u2013 McDowell County, North Carolina\nSkip to content\nSearch\nSearch for:\nMcDowell County Board of Elections\nMcDowell County, North Carolina\nMenu\nHome\nRegister to Vote\nVoting\nMcDowell County Precinct Sites, Maps and 2026 Notice of Buffer Zones\nFor Candidates\nCAMPAIGN FINANCE \u2013 ACTIVE COMMITTEES\nAbout Elections\nAbout the Board of Elections\nContact Us\nBoard Meetings/Minutes\nElection Results\nNorth Carolina State Board of Elections Website\nAssistance for Voters in Care Facilities\nMcDowell County Current Elected Officials\nOpen Search\nFeatured post\nFeatured\nNovember 3, 2026 Elections\nYour November 3, 2026 Ballot is available\nHERE!\n2026 McDowell Local Candidates\nDownload\n2026 Candidate Detail List\nUOCAVA Election Notice Updated 11.03.2026(3)\nDownload\nFeatured post\nFeatured\nMcDowell County Board of Elections \u2013 Current Updates\nFeatured post\nFeatured\nAbsentee By-Mail Voting\nAbsentee-By-Mail Voting\nAny North Carolina registered voter may request, receive, and vote a mail-in absentee ballot for the 2026 elections.\nRegistered voters in North Carolina must request an absentee ballot with an official NC Absentee Ballot Request Form. There are two ways to access and submit the form:\nOnline:\nOption 1 at the\nNC Absentee Ballot Portal\n.\nOn paper:\n2026 NC Absentee Ballot Request Form (fillable PDF)\n.\nAfter completing, submit the form to your\ncounty board of elections\nor in person or by mail via the U.S. Postal Service, DHL, FedEx, or UPS.\nThe deadline to request an absentee ballot is two weeks before Election Day; the deadline differs for\nmilitary and overseas citizen voters\n.\n2026_Absentee_Request_Form_Fillable_English\nDownload\nCommon ID Flyer-revised-08-13-2026 (1)\nDownload\nFeatured post\nFeatured\nRegistration Repair\nFind out if your voter registration is incomplete and how to repair it\n17 Jul 2025\nAssistance for Voters in Care Facilities\nhttps://www.ncsbe.gov/voting/help-voters-disabilities/assistance-voters-care-facilities\nIn McDowell County, please contact: Jane Propst, Director at 828-659-0834 or by email to\nelections@mcdowellnc.gov\n7 Aug 2024\n10 Facts Election Security in North Carolina\n10_Facts_Election_Security_NC_DIGITAL_April_2024\nDownload\n29 Jan 2024\nTogether NC Video Project\n24 Jan 2024\nNC Voter ID Information\nNotice About Photo ID Requirement for Voting\nVoters will now be asked to present a valid photo identification when voting in person. If you do not have a valid photo ID card, you may obtain one from your county board of elections prior to the election, through the end of the early voting period.\nIf you do not have a valid photo ID card on Election Day, you may still vote and have your vote counted by signing an affidavit of reasonable impediment (or \u201cPhoto ID Exception Form\u201d) as to why you have not presented a valid photo ID. The Exception Form can also be used if you have a religious objection to being photographed or are a victim of a recently declared natural disaster.\nAs an alternative, if you don\u2019t have your ID when you vote, you can still vote and then bring your valid photo ID to your county board of elections by noon on the third business day after Election Day.\nIf you vote by mail, except for military and overseas citizen voters, then you must include a photocopy of a valid photo ID when returning your ballot. You may also complete the Absentee Photo ID Exception Form that is provided with your absentee ballot materials.\nA list of all types of ID that can be used for voting is available on the State Board of Elections\nVoter ID\nwebpage. For information on how to get a free ID, see\nGet a Free Voter Photo ID\n.\nClick here for NC Voter ID Information\n10 Facts About NC\u2019s Photo ID Requirement for Voting\n23 May 2023\nVoting Maps and Redistricting\nClick Here to view the NC Voting Maps\n4 Mar 2022\nPosts navigation\nOlder posts\nMcDowell County Board of Elections\nMcDowell County Board of Elections\nBlog at WordPress.com.\nUp \u2191\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nMcDowell County Board of Elections\nSign me up\nHave a WordPress.com account?\nLog in now.\nMcDowell County Board of Elections\nView site in Reader\nManage subscriptions\nSign up\nLog in\nReport this content\nCollapse this bar\nLoading Comments...\nWrite a Comment...\nEmail\nName\nWebsite",
